 frq:{prompt:'A clinic plans to launch a patient portal after its vendor says it is secure. Explain how an administrator should translate applicable requirements into a practical implementation and review process.',rubric:[['Establish scope and ownership',['requirement','scope','owner']],['Separate privacy and security',['permission','access','security']],['Implement a usable workflow',['workflow','training','identity']],['Monitor and verify correction',['monitor','evidence','verify']]],model:'Identify which requirements apply to the clinic, service and vendor relationship, and assign owners with appropriate compliance input. Distinguish permission to use or disclose information from technical safeguards. Map identity checks, access roles, release decisions, account removal, downtime and escalation. Test realistic scenarios and train staff with the resources needed to follow the process. Monitor practice through appropriate samples and feedback, investigate gaps, assign corrective actions and verify their effectiveness. A vendor assurance or attendance record alone does not establish that the organization’s responsibilities have been met.'},
